1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,760
That cheap-ass car payment is quietly robbing you of five grand.

2
00:00:04,480 --> 00:00:07,540
Stretch your car loan from four years to seven, and the payment drops.

3
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:12,500
Like, three hundred ninety-five bucks a month. Sounds like a win, right? Hell no.

4
00:00:13,020 --> 00:00:17,860
You borrow about forty-four thousand seven hundred for a new car, the average loan, per Edmunds.

5
00:00:18,140 --> 00:00:22,160
The bank charges seven percent a year. That's interest, the fee for borrowing.

6
00:00:22,700 --> 00:00:25,200
Double-tap if you've ever signed without reading the total.

7
00:00:25,200 --> 00:00:28,240
Four years? About one thousand seventy a month.

8
00:00:28,760 --> 00:00:30,940
And about six thousand seven hundred in interest.

9
00:00:31,480 --> 00:00:33,860
Seven years? About six seventy-four a month.

10
00:00:34,260 --> 00:00:36,400
But almost twelve thousand in interest.

11
00:00:37,140 --> 00:00:41,280
Same damn car. About five thousand three hundred extra, straight to the bank.

12
00:00:41,820 --> 00:00:44,680
Send this to the friend who thinks a low payment means a good deal.

13
00:00:45,200 --> 00:00:48,900
At the typical wage, that's two hundred sixteen hours of your life.

14
00:00:49,400 --> 00:00:53,240
That's more than five full work weeks of clocking in, just for the longer loan.

15
00:00:53,240 --> 00:00:55,760
Save this before you ever sign one.

16
00:00:56,220 --> 00:00:59,240
And when it's finally paid off? Your car's already seven years old.

17
00:00:59,760 --> 00:01:02,900
Lower payment, bigger bill. The math doesn't care how it feels.

18
00:01:03,440 --> 00:01:05,420
Four years or seven, what's your car loan?

